bulkCreate returns string instead of Date in postgres
Issue Creation Checklist

 I understand that my issue will be automatically closed if I don't fill in the requested information
 I have read the contribution guidelines

Bug Description
When using Model.bulkCreate, DataTypes.DATE column is returning string.

Reproducible Example
class Post extends Model {
	declare id?: number;
	declare dateValue: Date;
}

Post.init(
	{
		id: { type: DataTypes.INTEGER, primaryKey: true, autoIncrement: true },
		dateValue: DataTypes.DATE,
	},
	{
		sequelize,
		modelName: "Post",
	},
);

const resCreate = await Post.create({ dateValue: new Date() });

const resCreateBulk = await Post.bulkCreate([{ dateValue: new Date() }]);
const resCreateBulk0 = resCreateBulk[0]!;

expect(resCreate.dateValue).to.be.instanceOf(Date);
// `dateValue` should be `Date`, but it's `string`
expect(resCreateBulk0.dateValue).not.to.be.instanceOf(Date);
expect(resCreateBulk0.dateValue).to.be.instanceOf(Date);
Here is the link to the SSCCE for this issue: link
I do not know why CI is returning success. It looks like it's not testing at all, since there are
this 2 lines in code, in which one will always fails
expect(resCreateBulk0.dateValue).not.to.be.instanceOf(Date);
expect(resCreateBulk0.dateValue).to.be.instanceOf(Date);
Also there is no SSCCE done without errors! or SSCCE done with error (see above). in logs.
What do you expect to happen?
dateValue should be Date when creating with bulkCreate

What is actually happening?
dateValue is string when creating with bulkCreate
dateValue is Date when creating with create

