IntelliJ IDEA run window fails to show all SoftAssertions errors in concurrent JUnit tests
Describe the bug
In my current test setup, I am using SoftAssertions within nested classes. After running such a test class with JUnit concurrency, individual test failures in the IntelliJ Run window do not correctly display. Although all assertion errors are logged, only one test failure is shown.

assertj core version: 3.26.3
java version: 22
test framework version: (JUnit 5) 5.11.0-M2
IntelliJ IDEA 2024.1.4 (Ultimate Edition)
os (if relevant): Windows 11

Test case reproducing the bug

Set the concurrency run parameters for JUnit.
Run the test class SoftAssertInConcurrentRunOfTests.
Observe the logs to see that three assertion errors are captured.
Check the IntelliJ Run window to see that only one test is marked as failed.

Concurrency run parameters:
junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.enabled = true
junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.config.strategy= dynamic
junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.mode.default = concurrent
junit.jupiter.execution.parallel.mode.classes.default = concurrent
import org.assertj.core.api.SoftAssertions;
import org.assertj.core.api.junit.jupiter.InjectSoftAssertions;
import org.assertj.core.api.junit.jupiter.SoftAssertionsExtension;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Nested;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.ExtendWith;

@ExtendWith({SoftAssertionsExtension.class})
public class SoftAssertInConcurrentRunOfTests {

    @InjectSoftAssertions
    private SoftAssertions softly;

    @Test
    void testInsideSimpleClass() {
        softly.assertThat(1).isEqualTo(2);
    }

    @Nested
    class NestedTestClass {
        @Test
        void testInsideNestedClass1() {
            softly.assertThat(1).isEqualTo(2);
        }
    }

    @Nested
    class NestedTestClass2 {
        @Test
        void testInsideNestedClass2() {
            softly.assertThat(1).isEqualTo(2);
        }
    }
}

The problem does not occur when SoftAssertions are injected individually for each test.
@Nested
    class NestedTestClass2 {
        @Test
        void testInsideNestedClass2(SoftAssertions softly) {
            softly.assertThat(1).isEqualTo(2);
        }
    }
If it is intended way how it works, it might be helpful to update documentation for usage of SoftAssertions with junit concurency/nested test classes.

