Add API for writing informational messages in tests
Description
My team uses seeded random value generation throughout our test suites. To ensure that tests are repeatable, we log the seed to the console before each test is run. With XCTest, we did this using XCTContext.runActivity as follows:
open class RandomizedTestCase : XCTestCase, RandomValueGeneratingTestSuite {
    …
    @MainActor
    public var randomSeed: UInt64 {
        …
        set {
            XCTContext.runActivity(named: "Using random seed \(newValue)") { (activity) in
                randomNumberGenerator.seed = newValue
                print(activity.name)
            }
        }
    }

    …

    open override func setUp() async throws {
        try await super.setUp()
        await setRandomSeed(Date.timeIntervalSinceReferenceDate.bitPattern)
    }
}
This allows the seed to show up in the console and xcresult bundles. In CI, we extract information from the xcresult bundles to generate HTML test reports, and it’s important that the seeds show up for failed tests so that engineers can repeat the test with the same inputs to diagnose what went wrong.
As best as I can tell, Swift Testing lacks any mechanism to log dynamic informational messages in tests. Console output is not included in the JSON ABI (or xcresult bundles when run from Xcode), so we can’t use print(…). Issue.record(_:sourceLocation:) nearly works, but issues are treated like test failures, which is inappropriate for our use case. If there were something like Message.record(_:sourceLocation:), that would probably work well for us.
Without some mechanism for seeing the random seeds in xcresult bundles, we can’t adopt Swift Testing.
If you consider this more an Xcode issue vs. a Swift Testing one, please let me know and I can log something using Feedback Assistant.
swift-testing version/commit hash
Whichever version is included with Xcode 16 beta 5.
Swift & OS version (output of swift --version && uname -a)
