LDC doesn't like this:
struct S
{
nothrow @nogc:

    alias toString this;

    const(char)* ptr;

    // comment this and the error goes away
    this(ref inout typeof(this) rhs) inout pure {}

    const(char)[] toString() const pure
        => ptr[0 .. ptr[-1]];
}

class Test
{
    S s;
    const(char)[] test()
    {
        return s;              // ERROR: this causes the error (result should coerce via alias-this)
//        return s.toString(); // WORKS: explicit call makes the error go away
    }
}
1>Function return type does not match operand type of return inst!
1>  ret ptr %3, !dbg !20962
1>COMPILED : { i64, ptr }LLVM error : Broken module found, compilation aborted!
1>Exception Code: 0xC000001D

Remove the copy constructor and this error goes away.
Alternatively, call toString explicitly rather than falling to alias-this also makes it go away.

