NiceGUI Vue Component does not call callback with large parameters
First Check

 I added a very descriptive title here.
 This is not a Q&A. I am sure something is wrong with NiceGUI or its documentation.
 I used the GitHub search to find a similar issue and came up empty.

Description
My environment

Windows11
Python v3.12.7
nicegui v2.13.0

Problem Summary
When using $emit in Vue component to trigger a Python callback, events are not emitted if the size of the parameters being passed is large.
While smaller parameters work correctly, when over about 1MB , the event does not trigger, and the Python callback is not invoked.
The test code is shown below.
Test Code Explanation:
The test uses the q-file component to select a file, encodes it in Base64, and passes this text to the Python callback.
When the Base64 encoded text exceeds around 1MB, the event stops triggering, and the Python callback is no longer called.
test.py
from nicegui import ui
from nicegui.element import Element

class TestComponent(Element, component="test.vue"):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.on("change_file", self._on_change_file)

    def _on_change_file(self, event):
        log.push(f"{event.args['name']} : {event.args['data']}")

ui.label("Event test")
TestComponent()
log = ui.log()

ui.run()
test.vue
<template>
    <q-file outlined v-model="model" @update:model-value="value => onFileChange(value)" />
</template>

<script>
export default {
    props: {
    },
    data() {
        return {
            model: null,
        }
    },
    mounted() {
    },
    methods: {
        onFileChange(e) {
            e.arrayBuffer().then((buffer) => {
                // encode to base64
                const base64 = btoa(
                    new Uint8Array(buffer)
                        .reduce((data, byte) => data + String.fromCharCode(byte), '')
                );
                console.log(base64);
                this.$emit('change_file', {
                    name: e.name,
                    data: base64
                });
            });
        },
