Crash when project depends on dyn_clone
Running cargo verus verify (using commit ec90cbaf857ab4f55f8a64f6b411554d51e73dab) on a project that depends on dyn_clone results in an internal Verus error, even when definitions from dyn_clone are not referenced in verified code:
$ cargo verus verify
   Compiling verus_sample v0.1.0
[rust_verify/src/lifetime_generate.rs:561:13] ty = dyn [Binder { value: Trait(dyn_clone::DynClone), bound_vars: [] }, Binder { value: AutoTrait(DefId(2:3407 ~ core[fafc]::marker::Sync)), bound_vars: [] }, Binder { value: AutoTrait(DefId(2:27213 ~ core[fafc]::marker::Send)), bound_vars: [] }] + 'clone/#0
thread 'rustc' panicked at rust_verify/src/lifetime_generate.rs:562:13:
unexpected type
note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace
error: could not compile `verus_sample` (bin "verus_sample")

This is src/main.rs:
use vstd::prelude::*;
#[allow(unused)]
use dyn_clone::DynClone;

verus! {
fn main() {
}
}

Here's the corresponding Cargo.toml:
[package]
name = "verus_sample"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
vstd = { path = "../verus/source/vstd" }
builtin = { path = "../verus/source/builtin" }
builtin_macros = { path = "../verus/source/builtin_macros" }
dyn-clone = "1.0.19"

[package.metadata.verus]
verify = true

As a workaround, it seems to work to add TyKind::Dynamic(..) => Box::new(TypX::Never), in lifetime_generate::erase_ty but I'm pretty sure that that's not the right fix and only works because dyn_clone is not actually used for any verified code.

Crash when using vkSetHdrMetadataEXT() under my Vulkan implementation on FLTK.
I am adding Vulkan support to FLTK.  It has been working fine, but I ran into an incompatibility between MoltenVK and FLTK's Cocoa.  Basically, trying to use vkSetHdrMetadataEXT() leads to a crash, on this FLTK's function:
double Fl_Darwin_System_Driver::wait(double time_to_wait)
{
if (dropped_files_list) { // when the list of dropped files is not empty, open one and remove it from list
drain_dropped_files_list();
}
NSAutoreleasePool *pool = [[NSAutoreleasePool alloc] init];
time_to_wait = Fl_System_Driver::wait(time_to_wait);
// the deprecation warnings can be ignored because they run only for macOS < 10.11
#pragma clang diagnostic push
#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-declarations"
if (fl_mac_os_version < 101100) NSDisableScreenUpdates(); // deprecated 10.11
Fl::flush();
if (fl_mac_os_version < 101100) NSEnableScreenUpdates(); // deprecated 10.11
#pragma clang diagnostic pop
if (Fl::idle) // 'idle' may have been set within flush()
time_to_wait = 0.0;
int retval = do_queued_events(time_to_wait);
Fl_Cocoa_Window_Driver::q_release_context();
[pool release];   /// <---------- THIS CRASHES when vkSetHdrMetadataEXT is used.
return retval;
}
Any ideas how to fix it?  For more info and for an FLTK vk_shape_hdr-shared program that shows the issue:
fltk/fltk#1250
